INT. ST. MARGARET HOSPITAL - NURSES STATION - NIGHT

The ward is quiet. The clock on the wall shows 3:10. A cleaner pushes a mop slowly past the station and does not look at anyone. In the corner a vending machine hums. PRIYA sits with a clipboard, DR. ALBERT eats a sandwich with great care, TOMASZ is looking at his phone and GLORIA, the night manager, walks in a circle around the desk with a mug in her hand and a smile that does not move.

PRIYA
(she closes the clipboard)
Everybody, tonight is very calm. Maybe the calmest night this year.

DR. ALBERT
(he chews, then points to the sandwich)
Please do not say this word. Calm. It is a bad word in hospital.

PRIYA
(laughing, she touches the wooden desk)
I am sorry. I take it back.

TOMASZ
(to himself, he reads the screen)
Again no message from my wife. Maybe she is sleeping.

ON PHONE: Tomek where r u? Come home early pls. Dog is sick.

TOMASZ
(he turns the phone to Priya)
You see? The dog. Always the dog.

PRIYA
(she reads and nods)
You have a dog? I thought you hate animals.

TOMASZ
(quietly, to the room)
I hate everything at three in the morning.

GLORIA
(she lifts the mug to all of them)
Friends, I am so happy with this team. Really. Look at this peace.

DR. ALBERT
(to Priya, low, he lowers the sandwich)
Why is she so happy? She is never happy.

PRIYA
(whispering, she shrugs)
Maybe she had good sleep.

GLORIA
(she hears and smiles wider)
I heard this. I am fine. Please, continue your work.

Two TEENAGERS in school jackets come through the doors, one holding a bloody paper towel to the other's chin. Nobody stands up. Priya waves them to the waiting chairs without looking, Tomasz types a reply with one thumb, and Dr. Albert hides the sandwich under a folder while Gloria walks to the window and looks down at the parking lot as if she is waiting for someone.

The desk phone RINGS. Priya answers.

PRIYA
(into the phone)
Ward four, Priya speaking.

DIRECTOR (V.O.)
(through the phone, calm and slow)
Priya, good evening. This is the Director, from the head office. I am downstairs. I am coming up to see your ward.

PRIYA
(she covers the receiver, to everyone)
It is the Director. He is downstairs.

DR. ALBERT
(he stands, the folder falls, the sandwich falls)
Ah no. No, no.

TOMASZ
(he puts the phone away and fixes his hair)
Now I understand why she smile.

GLORIA
(turning from the window, very quietly, to all)
He has been in the building since midnight. I did not tell you because I wanted to see your real work.

PRIYA
(into the phone, with a very small voice)
Welcome, Director. We are ready.

DIRECTOR (V.O.)
(the elevator DINGS behind the phone voice)
I know. I saw everything on the camera.

The elevator doors OPEN at the end of the corridor. The cleaner with the mop stops, takes off his cap, and looks at the four of them.

TOMASZ
(a whisper)
Is the cleaner the Director?

Nobody answers. The cleaner smiles.
